The résumé version of me is [here](/work) and [here](/projects). This is just the parts that don't fit in a bullet point:

- I over-engineer everything. Not because it's necessary - leaving something "good enough" alone genuinely bothers me.
- I've rewritten my own editor, my own IDE, and part of my own C++ dialect, mostly out of spite for tools that almost did what I wanted.
- Grew up in Hong Kong, studied in the UK, and still haven't decided which country's keyboard shortcuts I actually prefer.
- My homelab draws more power than it has any right to for what it actually does.
- I will bring up Nix in conversation whether or not it's relevant. [Ask](/writing/nix) [my friends](/writing/more-on-nix).
- Compilers are the one part of this field I'd happily do for free. Everything else is negotiable.

[Say hi](mailto:ujaandas03@gmail.com) - I like talking to people who build things too.
